Here is the implementation of getCommonCharacterCount function in JavaScript:

```js
function getCommonCharacterCount(s1, s2) {
  let count = 0;

  const s1Chars = new Set(s1.split(''));

  for (let char of s2) {
    if (s1Chars.has(char)) {
      count++;
      s1Chars.delete(char);
    }
  }

  return count;
}
```

The key steps are:

1. Split s1 into an array of characters using split('')
2. Create a Set from this array to get unique characters 
3. Loop through s2 
4. Check if each character of s2 is present in the Set
5. If yes, increment count and remove that character from Set
6. Return final count

This avoids nested loops and gives O(n+m) time complexity where n and m are lengths of two strings.

