Here is a function that takes in longitude and latitude coordinates and returns the features from those coordinates from a .pmtiles file:

```js
function getFeaturesFromCoordinates(lon, lat) {
  // Open pmtiles file
  const pmtiles = require('./path/to/pmtiles.json');

  // Find tile containing coordinates
  const tileZoom = 14; // Tile zoom level
  const x = Math.floor(lon/360 + 0.5) * Math.pow(2, tileZoom);
  const y = Math.floor((1 - Math.log(Math.tan(lat * Math.PI/180) + 1 / Math.cos(lat * Math.PI/180))/Math.PI) / 2 * Math.pow(2, tileZoom));

  // Get features from tile
  const tile = pmtiles.tiles[y][x];
  return tile.features;
}

// Example usage
const lon = -73.5;
const lat = 40.7;
const features = getFeaturesFromCoordinates(lon, lat);
```

This function:

- Requires the pmtiles file 
- Calculates the x/y tile coordinates from the longitude/latitude
- Looks up the tile object from the pmtiles data
- Returns the features array from that tile object

