Here is an updated function that loads the pmtiles data from a remote URL using the pmtiles:// protocol instead of requiring a local file:

```js
async function getFeaturesFromCoordinates(lon, lat) {
  // Load pmtiles from remote URL
  const response = await fetch(`pmtiles://example.com/data.pmtiles`);
  const pmtiles = await response.json();

  const tileZoom = 14;

  const x = Math.floor(lon/360 + 0.5) * Math.pow(2, tileZoom);
  const y = Math.floor((1 - Math.log(Math.tan(lat * Math.PI/180) + 1 / Math.cos(lat * Math.PI/180))/Math.PI) / 2 * Math.pow(2, tileZoom));

  const tile = pmtiles.tiles[y][x];
  return tile.features;
}

// Example usage
const lon = -73.5; 
const lat = 40.7;

getFeaturesFromCoordinates(lon, lat)
  .then(features => {
    // process features
  });
```

The main changes:

- Make the function async to support await
- Fetch the pmtiles data from a URL instead of requiring a local file 
- Handle the response as JSON
- Return a Promise instead of direct return

